. 
. ///// Ever changed treatment
> gen ever_change_d_XX=(abs(diff_from_sq_XX)>0&treatment_XX!=.)
352. replace ever_change_d_XX=1 if ever_change_d_XX[_n-1]==1&group_XX==group_XX[_n-1]
353. 
. ///// Creating date of first treatment change
> sort group_XX time_XX
354. gen temp_F_g_XX=time_XX if ever_change_d_XX==1&ever_change_d_XX[_n-1]==0 
355. replace temp_F_g_XX=0 if temp_F_g_XX==.
356. bys group_XX: gegen F_g_XX=max(temp_F_g_XX)
357. drop temp_F_g_XX
358. 
. ///// If continuous option specified, generating polynomials of D_{g,1},
> ///// storing D_{g,1} somewhere, and replacing it by 0.
> if `continuous'>0{
359.         
.         scalar degree_pol = `continuous'
360.         
. forvalues pol_level = 1/`=degree_pol'{
361.         scalar pol_level_XX = `pol_level'
362.         capture drop d_sq_`pol_level'_XX 
363.         gen d_sq_`pol_level'_XX = d_sq_XX^scalar(pol_level_XX)
364. }
365. capture drop d_sq_XX_orig
366. gen d_sq_XX_orig=d_sq_XX
367. replace d_sq_XX=0
368. }
369. 
. // Create a new variable = to d_sq_XX expressed in integers
. capture drop d_sq_int_XX
370. 
. gegen d_sq_int_XX = group(d_sq_XX)
371. 
. ///// Dropping the values of the baseline treatment such that no variance in F_g within those values.
> capture drop var_F_g_XX
372. bys d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen var_F_g_XX=sd(F_g_XX)
373. drop if var_F_g_XX==0
374. drop var_F_g_XX
375. 
. //// CHANGE BELOW - tks
> //// Counting number of groups after the drop above
> cap drop group2_XX
376. egen group2_XX = group(group_XX)
377. sum group2_XX
378. scalar G_XX=r(max)
379. ////
> 
. ///// Error message if Design Restriction 1 is not met.
> count
380. if r(N)==0{
381.         di as error ""
382.         di as error "No treatment effect can be estimated. This is because Design Restriction 1 in de Chaisemartin & D'Haultfoeuille (2
> 024) is not satisfied in the data, given the options requested. This may be due to the fact that groups' period-one treatment is continuou
> s, or takes a large number of values, and you have not specified the continuous option. If so, you can try to specify this option. If the 
> issue persists even with this option, this means that all groups experience their first treatment change at the same date, a situation whe
> re the estimators of de Chaisemartin & D'Haultfoeuille (2024) cannot be used."
383.         di as input _continue ""
384. 
.         exit
385. }
386. 
. ///// For each value of the baseline treatment, we drop time periods such that we do not have any control with that baseline treatment aft
> er that period
> ///// This means the panel is no longer balanced, though it is balanced within values of the baseline treatment
> gen never_change_d_XX=1-ever_change_d_XX
387. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen controls_time_XX=max(never_change_d_XX)
388. drop if controls_time_XX==0
389. 
. ///// Computing t_min_XX, T_max_XX, and replacing F_g_XX by last period plus one for those that never change treatment
> sum time_XX
390. scalar t_min_XX=r(min)
391. scalar T_max_XX=r(max)
392. replace F_g_XX=T_max_XX+1 if F_g_XX==0
393. 
. ///// Dealing with missing treatments: most conservative option
> 
. *Let FMD_g denote the first date when g's treatment is missing while y has been not missing at least once, so that we know for sure that g
>  already exists. If that date is before the first period when g's treatment changes, we do not know when g's treatment has changed for the
>  first time. Then, a conservative option is to drop all of g's outcomes starting at FMD_g.
. 
. if "`drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch'"!=""{
394. replace outcome_XX=. if min_time_d_miss_aft_ynm_XX<F_g_XX&time_XX>=min_time_d_miss_aft_ynm_XX
395. }
396. 
. ///// Dealing with missing treatments: most liberal option
> 
. *Let FD_g and LD_g respectively denote the first and last period where a group's treatment is non missing. Let FY_g denote the first perio
> d where a group's outcome is non missing.
. 
. *For groups that experience at least one treatment change, let LDBF_g denote the last date before F_g where g's treatment is non missing. 
> We have FD_g<=LDBF_g<F_g<=LD_g, and we will deal with missing treatments depending on when they occur with respect to those four dates.
. 
. capture drop last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX
397. capture drop last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX
398. gen last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX=time_XX if time_XX<F_g_XX&treatment_XX!=.
399. bys group_XX: gegen last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX=max(last_obs_D_bef_switch_t_XX)
400. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, we just have FD_g<=LD_g, and we will deal with missing treatments depending on when
>  they occur with respect to those two dates.
. 
. *For t<FD_g, by default we are going to consider that g joins the panel at FD_g: any non-missing outcome before FD_g replaced as missing, 
> but all non-missing outcomes after FD_g are kept. For groups such that FY_g<FD_g, this is a "liberal" convention: those groups exist befor
> e FD_g, so one could argue that their status quo treatment is missing and they should be dropped from the analysis. We give the user the o
> ption to do that, with drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch option
.   
. replace outcome_XX=. if time_XX<min_time_d_nonmiss_XX 
401. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at FD_g<t<LDBF_g, we replace their missing treatment by their status-quo t
> reatment. Again, this is a liberal convention, so we give the user the option to not use those observations, with drop_if_d_miss_before_fi
> rst_switch option.
. 
. replace treatment_XX=d_sq_XX if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX<last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX&time_XX>min_time_d_nonmiss_XX
402. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at LDBF_g<t<F_g (equivalent to LDBF_g<F_g-1), we cannot know the exact dat
> e when their treatment has changed, even in a binary and staggered design. Therefore, we set their outcomes at missing starting at LDBF_g+
> 1. We also redefine their F_g as T+1 because they are effectively control groups. We also define the trunc_control_XX as LDBF_g+1 for them
> , because they can only be used as controls till that date.
. 
. replace outcome_XX=. if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&time_XX>last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_XX-1
403. capture drop trunc_control_XX
404. gen trunc_control_XX=last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX+1 if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_XX-1
405. replace F_g_XX=T_max_XX+1 if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX<F_g_XX-1
406. 
. *For groups that experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at F_g<t, we replace their missing treatment by D(g,F_g). This is again a 
> liberal convention, but it is innocuous for the reduced-form parameters DID_l, so we do not give the user the option to overrule it (Note 
> that overruling it could make the same_switchers option fail)
. 
. gen d_F_g_temp_XX = treatment_XX if time_XX==F_g_XX
407. bys group_XX: gegen d_F_g_XX = mean(d_F_g_temp_XX)
408. replace treatment_XX=d_F_g_XX if F_g_XX<T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX>F_g_XX&last_obs_D_bef_switch_XX==F_g_XX-1
409. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, if D_gt missing at FD_g<t<LD_g, we replace their missing treatment by D_g1. This is
>  again a liberal convention, so we give the user the option to not use those observations, with drop_if_d_miss_before_first_switch option.
. 
. replace treatment_XX=d_sq_XX if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1&treatment_XX==.&time_XX>min_time_d_nonmiss_XX&time_XX<max_time_d_nonmiss_XX
410. 
. *For groups that do not experience a treatment change, we replace all their outcomes by missing at t>LD_g. Even in a binary and staggered 
> design, we cannot infer their treatment at t>LD_g.
. 
. replace outcome_XX=. if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1&time_XX>max_time_d_nonmiss_XX
411. replace trunc_control_XX=max_time_d_nonmiss_XX+1 if F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1
412. 
. ///// Store the outcome in levels, will be useful later when predict_het and trends_lin specified
> if "`predict_het_good'"!=""{
413. gen outcome_non_diff_XX=outcome_XX
414. }
415. 
. ///// If trends_lin option specified, drop units for which F_g_XX==2, and redefine 
> ///// outcome and controls in first difference.
> if "`trends_lin'"!=""{
416.         drop if F_g_XX==2
417.         xtset group_XX time_XX
418.         capture drop FD_outcome_XX
419.         gen FD_outcome_XX =outcome_XX-L.outcome_XX
420.         replace outcome_XX = FD_outcome_XX
421.         drop FD_outcome_XX
422.         
.         // adapt controls for case where trends_lin by and continuous specified together
.         if "`trends_lin'"!=""&"`by'"!=""&`continuous'!=0{
423.         local controls = "`controls_orig_XX'"
424. }
425.         
.         if "`controls'" !=""{
426.         foreach var of varlist `controls'{
427.         capture drop FD_`var'_XX
428.         gen FD_`var'_XX =`var' -L.`var'
429.         replace `var' = FD_`var'_XX
430.         drop FD_`var'_XX
431.         }
432.         }
433.         drop if time_XX==1
434.         sum time_XX
435.         scalar t_min_XX=r(min)
436. }
437. 
. ///// Balancing the panel
> cap rename _merge _merge_og
438. fillin group_XX time_XX
439. capture drop d_sq_XX_new
440. bys group_XX: gegen d_sq_XX_new=mean(d_sq_XX)
441. drop d_sq_XX
442. rename d_sq_XX_new d_sq_XX
443. 
. ///// CHANGE BELOW - tks
> 
. bys group_XX: gegen d_sq_int_XX_new = mean(d_sq_int_XX)
444. drop d_sq_int_XX
445. rename d_sq_int_XX_new d_sq_int_XX
446. 
. bys group_XX: gegen F_g_XX_new = mean(F_g_XX)
447. drop F_g_XX
448. rename F_g_XX_new F_g_XX
449. 
. /////
> 
. ///// Defining N_gt, the weight of each cell (g,t)
> gen N_gt_XX=1
450. replace N_gt_XX = N_gt_XX*weight_XX  //
451. replace N_gt_XX=0 if outcome_XX==.|treatment_XX==.
452. 
. ///// Determining last period where g still has a control group:
> ///// There is still a group with same 
> ///// treatment as g's in period 1 and whose treatment has not changed since 
> ///// start of panel. Definition adapted from the paper, to account for 
> ///// imbalanced panel.
> 
. capture drop F_g_trunc_XX
453. gen F_g_trunc_XX=F_g_XX
454. replace F_g_trunc_XX=min(F_g_XX,trunc_control_XX) if trunc_control_XX!=.
455. bys d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam': gegen T_g_XX = max(F_g_trunc_XX) 
456. replace T_g_XX = T_g_XX-1
457. 
. ///// Defining S_g: 
> ///// an indicator variable for groups whose average post switch 
> ///// treatment value is larger than their initial treatment D_{g,1}. 
> ///// They will be considered switchers in. If S_g==0, the group is a switcher out. 
> ///// For never-switchers, S_g is undefined.
> ///// Definition of S_g matches that in paper, unless dont_drop_larger_lower specified.
> 
. bys group_XX : gegen avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp = total(treatment_XX) if time_XX>=F_g_XX&time_XX<=T_g_XX
458. gen count_time_post_switch_XX_temp=(treatment_XX!=.) if time_XX>=F_g_XX&time_XX<=T_g_XX
459. bysort group_XX : gegen count_time_post_switch_XX=total(count_time_post_switch_XX_temp)
460. replace avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp =avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp/count_time_post_switch_XX
461. bys group_XX: gegen avg_post_switch_treat_XX=mean(avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp)
462. drop avg_post_switch_treat_XX_temp
463. 
. // When a group is a switching group, but its average post-treatment treatment 
. // value is exactly equal to its baseline treatment, we cannnot classify it as 
. // a swicher in or a switcher out, but it is not a control either. 
. // As such, we drop it from the estimation. Those groups are referred to 
. // as no-first-stage-switchers. This issue can only arise 
. // if dont_drop_larger_lower specified. 
. // if continuous is specified we do this according to the original 
. // baseline treatment and not to the one set to 0 to correctly
. // track if a group is switcher in or switcher out.
. if `continuous'==0{
464.         drop if avg_post_switch_treat_XX==d_sq_XX&F_g_XX!=T_g_XX+1
465.         gen S_g_XX=(avg_post_switch_treat_XX>d_sq_XX) if F_g_XX!=T_max_XX+1
466. }
467. else if `continuous'>0{
468.         drop if avg_post_switch_treat_XX==d_sq_XX_orig&F_g_XX!=T_g_XX+1
469.         gen S_g_XX=(avg_post_switch_treat_XX>d_sq_XX_orig) if F_g_XX!=T_max_XX+1
470. }       
471. // correct for the fact that if all avg_post_switch_treat_XX are missing it is considered as +inf
. egen aux_XX = min(avg_post_switch_treat_XX), by(group_XX)
472. replace S_g_XX = . if aux_XX ==.
473. 
. // Define another version where S_g=-1 for switchers out, which we need 
. // when predict_het or continuous specified.
. if "`predict_het_good'"!="" | `continuous'>0{
474. gen S_g_het_XX=S_g_XX
475. replace S_g_het_XX=-1 if S_g_het_XX==0
476. if "`predict_het_good'"!=""{
477. scalar heterogeneity_scalar_XX=1
478. }
479. }
480. 
. 
. ///// If continuous option specified: binarizing and staggerizing treatment,
> ///// and adding time_FEs interacted with D_{g,1} as controls
> if `continuous'>0{
481. 
. //Binarizing and staggerizing treatment
. capture drop treatment_XX_temp
482. gen treatment_XX_temp = (F_g_XX<=time_XX)*S_g_het_XX if S_g_het_XX!=.
483. capture drop treatment_XX_orig
484. gen treatment_XX_orig=treatment_XX
485. replace treatment_XX = treatment_XX_temp 
486. 
. //Enriching controls
. tab time_XX, gen(time_fe_XX_)
487. local max_time_XX=r(r)
488. // Modif Clément: actually, to compute the estimator with the continuous option we need to control for polynomial in D_{g,1} interacted
>  with \sum_{k=1}^t'1\{t=k}, sum of period FEs up to t'.
. forvalue i=2/`max_time_XX'{
489. replace time_fe_XX_`i'=(time_XX>=`i')
490. }
491. // End modif Clément
. foreach var of varlist time_fe_XX_2-time_fe_XX_`max_time_XX'{
492.         forvalues pol_level = 1/`=degree_pol'{
493.                 gen `var'_bt`pol_level'_XX = `var'*d_sq_`pol_level'_XX
494.                 local controls "`controls' `var'_bt`pol_level'_XX"
495.         }
496.         capture drop `var'
497. }
498. capture drop time_fe_XX_1
499. }
500. 
. ///// Creating treatment at F_g: D_{g,F_g}
> gen d_fg_XX_temp=treatment_XX if time_XX==F_g_XX
501. bys group_XX: gegen d_fg_XX=mean(d_fg_XX_temp)
502. replace d_fg_XX=d_sq_XX if d_fg_XX==. & F_g_XX==T_max_XX+1
503. drop d_fg_XX_temp 
504. 
. ///// Creating the variable L_g_XX = T_g_XX - F_g_XX, so that we can compute L_u or L_a afterwards.
> gen L_g_XX = T_g_XX - F_g_XX +1
505. 
. ///// Creating the equivalent variable L_g_placebo_XX for the placebos.
> if `placebo'!=0{
506. capture drop L_g_placebo_XX
507. gen L_g_placebo_XX = min(L_g_XX, F_g_XX-2) if F_g_XX>=3
508. }
509. 
. ///// Tagging first observation of each group_XX.
> sort group_XX time_XX
510. bysort group_XX : gen first_obs_by_gp_XX = (_n==1)
511. 
. ///// If cluster option specified, tagging first observation of each cluster, 
> ///// and checking clustering variable weakly coarser than group variable.
> 
. if "`cluster'"!=""{
512.                 
.         // FELIX 06-03-25 -> I guess this is how Tom solved it 
.         cap drop cluster_group_XX
513.         bysort group_XX: gegen cluster_group_XX=min(`cluster') 
514.         bysort group_XX: replace `cluster'=cluster_group_XX if `cluster'==.
515.         // Can do this because clusters have to be coarser than groups
.         
.         capture drop cluster_var_g_XX
516.         
.         bysort `cluster' (group_XX time_XX) : gen first_obs_by_clust_XX = (_n==1) if `cluster'!=. // FELIX 05_03_25 -> This is then not ne
> eded anymore
517.         
.         //Error message for clustering: non-nested case
.         bysort group_XX: gegen cluster_var_g_XX = sd(`cluster')
518.         sum cluster_var_g_XX
519.         scalar max_cluster_var_XX = `r(max)'
520.         if (scalar(max_cluster_var_XX) >0){
521.         di as error ""
522.         di as error "The group variable should be nested within the clustering variable."
523.         di as input _continue ""
524.         exit
525.         }
526.         
. }
527. 
. ///// Declaring data as panel //
> xtset group_XX time_XX
528. 
. ///// Creating first-differenced outcome and treatment//
> capture drop diff_y_XX
529. capture drop diff_d_XX
530. gen diff_y_XX = d.outcome_XX
531. g diff_d_XX = d.treatment_XX
532. 
. ////////// 3. Necessary pre-estimation steps when the controls option is specified.     
> 
. if "`controls'" !=""{
533. local count_controls=0
534. 
. capture drop fd_X_all_non_missing_XX
535. gen fd_X_all_non_missing_XX=1
536. 
. foreach var of varlist `controls'{
537. 
. local count_controls=`count_controls'+1
538. 
. capture drop diff_X`count_controls'_XX
539. capture drop avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX
540. capture drop resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX
541. 
. ///// Computing the first differences of the control variables
> 
. xtset group_XX time_XX
542. gen diff_X`count_controls'_XX=D.`var'
543. replace fd_X_all_non_missing_XX=0 if diff_X`count_controls'_XX==.
544. }
545. 
. ///// Residualization, and computation of term entering variance. 
> 
. local count_controls=0
546. local mycontrols_XX ""
547. local prod_controls_y ""
548. 
. foreach var of varlist `controls'{
549. local count_controls=`count_controls'+1
550. 
. capture drop sum_weights_control_XX //So as to consider the weighted regressions.
551. 
. // Computing  \Delta X_{.,t}: average of controls' first difference at time t, 
. // among groups whose treatment has not changed yet.
. 
. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : gegen sum_weights_control_XX = total(N_gt_XX) if ever_change_d_XX==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_mis
> sing_XX==1
552. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : gegen avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX = total(N_gt_XX*diff_X`count_controls'_XX) if ever_change_d
> _XX==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_missing_XX==1
553. 
. bys time_XX d_sq_XX `trends_nonparam' : replace avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX = avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX/sum_weights_control_XX
554. 
. // Computing \Delta\Dot{X}_{g,t}, the difference between the first differences 
. // of covariates and the average of their first-difference, which gives us 
. // the residuals of a regression of covariates on time fixed effects. 
. //Multiply by sqrt(N_gt_XX) to replicate weighted regression.
. 
. gen resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX = sqrt(N_gt_XX)*(diff_X`count_controls'_XX - avg_diff_X`count_controls'_XX)
555. 
. replace resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX=0 if resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX==.
556. 
. // Storing the obtained residuals for the computation of theta_d
. local mycontrols_XX "`mycontrols_XX' resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX"
557. 
. // Generating the product between \Delta\Dot{X}_{g,t} and \Delta Y_{g,t}
. //Multiply by sqrt(N_gt_XX) to replicate weighted regression
. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX
558. // Delete those we do not need anymore
. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_diff_y_temp_XX
559. capture drop prod_X`count_controls'_diff_y_XX
560. capture drop diff_y_wXX
561. gen diff_y_wXX = sqrt(N_gt_XX)*diff_y_XX
562. 
. * Note: resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX is already multiplied by sqrt(N_gt_XX)
. gen prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX=resid_X`count_controls'_time_FE_XX*sqrt(N_gt_XX)
563. replace prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX=0 if prod_X`count_controls'_Ngt_XX==. 
564. 
. }
565. 
. ///// Computing the Den_d matrices and their inverts,
> ///// and creating locals storing the status quos for which Den_d^{-1} not defined. 
> 
. local store_singular_XX ""
566. local store_noresidualization_XX ""
567. local levels_d_sq_XX_final ""
568. 
. levelsof d_sq_int_XX, local(levels_d_sq_XX)
569. 
. foreach l of local levels_d_sq_XX {
570.         
. capture drop E_y_hat_gt_int_`l'_XX              
571. 
. // Running residualization regression to compute predicted values
. 
. local controlsXX ""
572. forv i = 1/`count_controls'{
573.         local controlsXX "`controlsXX' diff_X`i'_XX"
574. }
575. 
. *Modif Clément 30/6/2025
. *cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
. if "`trends_nonparam'" == "" {
576. cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
577. }
578. if "`trends_nonparam'" != "" {
579. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
580. gegen trends_nonparam_temp_XX=group(`trends_nonparam')  
581. cap reg diff_y_XX `controlsXX' ibn.time_XX#ibn.trends_nonparam_temp_XX [aw=N_gt_XX] if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX, noconst
582. }
583. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. 
. if (_rc == 0) {
584. predict E_y_hat_gt_int_`l'_XX if d_sq_int_XX==`l'&time_XX<F_g_XX
585. *Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
586. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025
.         tempfile data_XX
587.         save "`data_XX'.dta", replace
588.         
. // A baseline treatment is relevant iff it is taken by at least two groups with different values of F_g_XX
. // and non-missing diff_y_XX, otherwise we do not need to perform the residualization for this specific baseline treatment.
. 
. scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 0 
589. tab F_g_XX if d_sq_int_XX==`l'  
590. 
. scalar useful_res_`l'_XX = `r(r)'
591.         if (scalar(useful_res_`l'_XX)>1){
592. 
. // Isolate the observations used in the computation of theta_d
. 
. keep if ever_change_d_XX==0&diff_y_XX!=.&fd_X_all_non_missing_XX==1&d_sq_int_XX==`l'
593. 
. // Using the matrix accum function, to regress the first difference of outcome on the first differences of covariates. We will obtain the 
> vectors of coefficients \theta_d s, where d indexes values of the baseline treatment.
. 
. capture matrix accum overall_XX = diff_y_wXX `mycontrols_XX'
594. scalar rc_XX=_rc
595. 
. if scalar(rc_XX)!=0{
596. scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 1
597. local store_noresidualization_XX "`store_noresidualization_XX' `l'"
598. scalar useful_res_`l'_XX=1
599. }
600. 
. else {
601.         
. // Isolate the parts of the matrix we need
. matrix didmgt_XX = overall_XX[2..`=`count_controls'+1',2..`=`count_controls'+1']
602. matrix didmgt_Xy = overall_XX[2..`=`count_controls'+1',1]
603. 
. // Computing the vectors of coefficients \theta_d s for each value of the baseline treatment
. matrix coefs_sq_`l'_XX = invsym(didmgt_XX)*didmgt_Xy
604. local levels_d_sq_XX_final "`levels_d_sq_XX_final' `l'" // Added local so as to avoid adding to the final block non-existent coefficien
> ts.
605. 
.                 // Computing the matrix Den^{-1}_d
.                         //Check first if the matrix is invertible, invsym() inverts a matrix even if it is singular
.                         capture drop scalar det_XX
606.                         scalar det_XX = det(didmgt_XX)
607. 
.                 if (abs(scalar(det_XX))<=10^(-16)){ 
608.                                         scalar store_singular_`l'_XX = 1
609.                                         scalar drop det_XX
610.                 }
611. 
.                 // Changes Diego 27-03-25: N_c_`l'_XX adjustment
.                 sum F_g_XX
612.                 gen N_c_`l'_temp_XX = time_XX >= 2 & time_XX <= r(max) - 1 & time_XX < F_g_XX & diff_y_XX < .
613.                 sum N_gt_XX if N_c_`l'_temp_XX == 1
614. 
.                 matrix inv_Denom_`l'_XX = invsym(didmgt_XX)*r(sum)*G_XX
615.                 drop N_c_`l'_temp_XX
616. }
617. 
. use "`data_XX'.dta", clear
618. 
. }
619. }
620. else {
621. *Modif Clément 19/6/2025
. capture drop trends_nonparam_temp_XX
622. *End Modif Clément 19/6/2025   
.     drop if d_sq_int_XX == `l'
623.     noi di "Baseline Treatment Level `l' dropped because of insufficient observations."
624. }
625. 
. }
626. 
. //Fill up store_singular_XX, with correct values of statu quo and not the levels -> Modif Felix
. levelsof d_sq_XX, local(levels_d_sq_bis_XX)
627. scalar index_sing_XX = 0
628. foreach l of local levels_d_sq_bis_XX {
629.         scalar index_sing_XX = scalar(index_sing_XX)+1
630.         capture confirm scalar store_singular_`=index_sing_XX'_XX
631.         if _rc==0{
632.                 if(scalar(store_singular_`=index_sing_XX'_XX) == 1){
633.                 local store_singular_XX = "`store_singular_XX' `l'"
634.                 }
635.         }
636. }
637. 
. ///// Display errors if one of the Den_d^{-1} is not defined
> if ("`store_singular_XX'"!=""){
638.         
.         di as error "Some control variables are not taken into account for groups with baseline treatment equal to: [`store_singular_XX']"
639.         di as error "This may occur in the following situations:"
640.         di as error "1. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, the regression of the outcome first difference on the c
> ontrols' first differences and time fixed effects has fewer observations than variables. Note that for each value of the baseline treatmen
> t, those regressions are estimated among (g,t)s such that g has not changed treatment yet at t."
641.         di as error "2. For groups with those values of the baseline treatment, two or more of your control variables are perfectly col
> linear in the sample where the regression is run, for instance because those control variables do not vary over time."
642.         di as input _continue ""
643. }
644. 
. ///// Values of baseline treatment such that residualization could not be performed at all are dropped.
> foreach l of local store_noresidualization_XX {
645. drop if d_sq_int_XX==`l'
646. }
647. 
. } // end of the if "`controls'" !="" condition
